ney.py::round_money used ROUND_HALF_UP even though its docstring says banker's rounding.\n\nChange: switch the quantize rounding mode to ROUND_HALF_EVEN and update the import accordingly. No other code changes.\n\nVerification: CI run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "fin-212-half-even-pr"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the nightly failure and opened PR #101 against main, with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py` imported and used `ROUND_HALF_UP` even though its docstring (per FIN-212) says banker's rounding. I checked the test values: 2.675 \u2192 2.68 and 2.665 \u2192 2.66 are the ROUND_HALF_EVEN results.\n- **Change:** On branch `fix/fin-212-half-even-rounding`, I switched the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` in `src/money.py`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI did not merge it. Merging into main needs code-owner approval under the organizational policy, so the PR is waiting on that.", "type": "text"}]}]}